0280                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character from
0280                             ; 60h to 7Eh is one of the escapes at pesc; "/" plus any other character
0280                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, and / then DEL gives "?"; "/',
0280                             ; '"' and '?' have no bit 6, so //, /" and /? give themselves).
0280                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    H_PRINT:   JMP   prlp   ; (the loop is with the escapes, out of the
                    PRLOOP:   EQU   prlp   ;   way of the handlers, which must fit in
                    PRAGAIN:   EQU   prlp   ;   the image's first two pages)
0280                          ENDIF      
0280                          IF   CHECKED   
0280                             ; (The checked build has the loop as a routine, prstr, which the error
0280                             ; report uses too. The address is kept meanwhile, for a report: it shows
0280                             ; the stack as it was before the "$". /~ comes back to hp1.)
